# Trivy ignore file — accepted HIGH advisories (0 CRITICAL) in the runtime images.
# Reviewed 2026-06-21 (see docs/production-readiness/risk-register.md PR-014). The Trivy gate is
# BLOCKING (deploy-checks.yml exit-code 1); every entry is an explicit, justified acceptance and the
# gate still FAILS on any NEW package/advisory not listed here (allowlist model, like .secrets.baseline).
#
# OS/debian base layers scan 0 HIGH/CRITICAL. `npm prune --omit=dev` in apps/{api,web}/Dockerfile
# removes the dev-only build tooling it CAN remove — glob (CVE-2025-64756) and tmp (CVE-2026-44705) are
# verified GONE (adding them here changed the count by 0), so they are intentionally NOT listed and the
# gate will fail if they reappear. Only advisories that genuinely persist in the image are accepted:
#
# ── picomatch (transitive, ReDoS; survives prune via @nestjs/cli -> @angular-devkit / chokidar hoist) ──
# HIGH, 0 CRITICAL, not on the request path. FOLLOW-UP: pin picomatch -> 4.0.4 via npm override.
CVE-2026-33671
